Package: ggboundary
Title: Trajectories Against Moving Boundaries (Safe Operating Space over Time)
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Rendell", "de Kort", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "rendell@c-economics.com")
Description: A small grammar for boundary visualisations built on 'ggplot2'.
    Its core is a value trajectory read against a boundary that may itself be
    fixed or move over time, with overshoot and slack shaded on ordinary
    Cartesian coordinates. Most "safe operating space" frameworks draw the
    boundary as a fixed line; a complex-adaptive-systems view treats the safe
    threshold as endogenous, so the boundary is a data series in its own right.
    The package also ships the static Doughnut Economics chart (a polar
    snapshot of the same primitives) and an expressive conch spiral for
    communication and physical data objects, both documented as companions to
    the Cartesian view rather than substitutes for it. Primitives: boundary
    (scalar or series), trajectory, safe band, overshoot, slack, zone of
    uncertainty. Keywords: doughnut economics, planetary boundaries, resilience,
    safe operating space, adaptive capacity.
